  "source_conclusion": "The existing federated cluster JUnit passes and reaches the exact named dn0 DataNode.deleteBlockPool guard twice. Its refreshNamenodes step stops and joins the removed block-pool service, then synchronously removes bpid2 from the manager before either delete request. The pinned pretarget heartbeat IOException is caught and retried and does not retain or reinsert that map entry; a client delete RPC IOException can erase a selected server occurrence. No reviewed existing JUnit plus the current typed-I/O fault model both changes that predicate and retains the selected request. This is a scoped test/fault-model suitability limit, not a claim that the production branch is unreachable or a completed fault campaign.",
